contentEn:
When a woman complains of some troubles that typically start 4-5 days before periods and almost continue during periods, she has Premenstrual Syndrome. It is largely because of hormonal imbalance. 

*Diagnosis:*
Most of the women have two types of symptoms - 
1.Emotional - Mood swings, irritability, anger, anxiety, depression, crying spells, poor concentration, insomnia, changes in libido, etc.
2.Physical - Body aches, pain in abdomen, headache, bodyaches, loose motions or constipation, bloating, fatigue, weakness, weight gain due to fluid retention, breast tenderness, etc.

*MANAGEMENT:*
The management can be in two parts - Drug management, and Lifestyle modifications. 

*A. Drug Management:*
Usually following four groups of drugs are used - 

*1. Anti-ovulatory medicines:*
As the problem starts after ovulation, use drugs that prevent ovulation. These fall in 3 groups - 

_a. Anti-ovulatory drugs -_ These include - 
• Vidang - Ghan Tab;
• Pippali - Ghan Tab;
• Tankan - kshar. 

Note: All these three drugs are present in  Garbha-anasthspak yoga.

_b. Anti-fertility drugs -_ These include - 
• Apamarg - Ghan Tab;
• Pudina - Jeevan Rasayan Ark;
• Jambhiri seeds; 
• Hapusha - Ghan Tab;
• Methi churna.

_c. Anti-implantation drugs -_ These include - 
• Japa-pushpa - Ghan Tab;
• Tulasi - Tulasi Ark, Tulasi ghan tab;
• Ark - patra churna;
• Mehndi - patra churna;
• Erand seeds - churna;
• Amaltas seeds - churna;
• Palash seeds - Palash ghan tab. 

*2. Neuro-tropic drugs:*
Because of the presence of emtional symptoms in PMS, use the following 2 groups of drugs - 

_a. Anti-depressant drugs -_ If the patient has depression, use anti-depressant drugs, like - 
• Jyotishmati - Tail, Rasayan, Ghan Tab;
• Kapikachhu - Ghan Tab;
• Ashwagandha - Ghan Tab 
• Gandira - Ghan Tab. 

_b. Anti-anxiety drugs -_ If the patient has anxiety, use anti-anxiety drugs, like - 
• Brahmi - Ghan Tab, Stresyl Tablet;
• Mandukparni - Ghan Tab;
• Ashwagandha - Ghan Tab;
• Shankhpushpi - Ghan Tab;
• Tagar - Ghan Tab, Stresyl Tablet. 

*3. Diuretic drugs:*
Because of the fluid retention in the body, the patient has weight gain and swollen hands and feet. To expel the water, use 
• Kakmachi - Ark, Ghan Tab;
• Sahdevi - Ghan Tab;
• Kasani - Ghan Tab;
• Punarnava - Ghan Tab;
• Gokshura - Ghan Tab.

 *4. Anti-inflammatory drugs:*
Because of the presence of generalised body pains, headache, etc. retention in the body, use - 
• Guggulu - Gokshuradi, Revplaq Tab;
• Shallaki - Shuddha Tab, Loswel Tab;
• Erandmula - Ghan Tab;
• Bilva-patra - Ghan Tab;
• Bhallatak - Ghan Tab, Revplaq Tab;
• Rasna - Ghan Tab.

*B. Lifestyle modifications:*
Following lifestyle modifications help a lot in alleviating the symptoms of PMS -
1.Avoid tok much of sugar, fats, salt and their products;
2.Eat complex whole grains;
3.Stay active and take regular exercise;
4.Do pranayam;
5.Do meditation;
6.Avoid smoking and drinking;
7.Eat calcium rich foods;
8.Follow ideal behavior.

