*Rasna is useful in many diseases*
Ayurveda regards Rasna as an excellent Amapachan, which is useful in many diseases, like - 
• Vata disorders (वात रोगाः);
• Amavata (आमवातः);
• Vata-rakta (वातरक्तः);
• Vataja shula (वातज शूलः);
• Gridhrasi (गृध्रसी);
• Shotha (शोथः);
• Shvasa (श्वास-रोगः);
• Kasa (कासः);
• Jvara (ज्वरः);
• Visha (विषः);
• Udar roga (उदर रोगः); etc.

*Rasna is useful in 80 Vata disorders*
However, above all, Ayurveda regards Rasna as the most effective drug (रास्ना वातहराणाम्) in 80 types of Vata rogas. Because of this action, Rasna is widely used for the management of almost all types of Vata disorders.

*Scientific Research*
Scientific research on Rasna carried out over the last several decades has shown that Rasna possesses following activities - 
1.  Analgesic (वेदनाहर);
2.  Anti-inflammatory (शोथहर);
3.  Antipyretic (ज्वरघ्न); 
4.  Immuno-modulator (आमविषहर)।

All these activities result from the modulation of immunity, inhibition of inflammatory mediators, and blockage of pain signals.

It is quite possible that the above-mentioned four activities of Rasna make it useful in the management of - 
1.  Neurological disorders; 
2.  Auto-immune disorders; and 
3.  Inflammatory diseases. 

*USAGE (उपयोग):*
On the basis of the ancient wisdom of ayurveda and modern scientific research, Rasna could be used in the management of - 
1.  Rheumatoid arthritis (आमवात);
2.  Ankylosing spondylitis   
     (आमविषज त्रिक-पृष्ठ-कटिग्रह);
3.  Osteo-arthritis (सन्धिवात);
4.  Fibromyalgia (सर्वांग-रुक्);
5.  Cervical spondylosis (ग्रीवा-वात);
6.  Lumbar spondylosis (कटिवात);
7.  Low Back Pain (कटिशूल);
8.  Sciatica (गृध्रसी); etc.

*Availability*
You can use Rasna in following forms - 
• Rasna churna - 3-6 gms, three times a day;
• Rasna kvath - 10-15 gms coarse powder, made into kvath, three times a day;
• Rasna-saptak kvath - 10-15 gms coarse powder, made into kvath, three times a day;
• Rasna Ghan Tab - Each Rasna Ghan Tab is made of 600 mg ghan (extract) derived from 3 gm dried powder of Rasna leaves. Start Rasna Ghan Tablet in the dose of 1-2 tabs, 3-6 times a day, with plain water. On improvement, taper off the dose. 
